  "title": "AI in energy works in pilots. Now it needs to work in operations.",
  "summary": "Across the energy and utilities sector, billions have been invested in artificial intelligence, yet most organizations are still struggling to move beyond pilots. The conversation is now shifting from experimentation to industrialization. The question is no longer whether AI can add value, but how to embed it into the core operational fabric of the enterprise in a way that is trusted, governed and built to last.",
